<%- include('./partials/header.ejs', { pageTitle: "Support | Smart Page Monitor" }) -%>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container narrow-container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Help center</p>
        <h1>Smart Page Monitor Support</h1>
        <p>
          Find answers to common questions and troubleshooting
          steps for the Smart Page Monitor extension.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container support-layout">
        <div class="support-content">
          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>Getting started</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>
                Open the webpage you want Smart Page Monitor to
                watch.
              </li>
              <li>
                Select the Smart Page Monitor icon in your
                browser toolbar.
              </li>
              <li>
                Select the button to begin monitoring the
                current page.
              </li>
              <li>
                The page will appear in your monitor list.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </article>
          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>Notifications are not appearing</h2>
            <p>Check the following:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Notifications are enabled in Smart Page Monitor
                settings.
              </li>

              <li>
                The extension has the Chrome
                <strong>notifications</strong> permission.
              </li>

              <li>
                Chrome is allowed to send notifications in your
                operating-system settings.
              </li>

              <li>
                Do Not Disturb or Focus Assist is not hiding
                notifications.
              </li>

              <li>
                The monitored page has actually changed since
                its previous successful check.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>A page is not being detected correctly</h2>

            <p>
              Some webpages load content dynamically, require a
              login, use anti-bot protection, or display
              different information for different visitors.
              These pages may not be monitored reliably.
            </p>

            <p>
              Try checking the monitor manually. If the problem
              continues, contact support and include the webpage
              URL and the error displayed by the extension.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>How often are pages checked?</h2>

            <p>
              New monitors use the default check interval chosen
              in the extension settings. The actual check time
              may vary slightly because of server load, browser
              availability, or website response time.
            </p>

            <p>
              Changing the default interval affects newly
              created monitors unless the extension specifically
              provides a way to edit existing monitors.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>How do I delete a monitor?</h2>

            <p>
              Open Smart Page Monitor, select the monitor from
              the list, and choose the delete option on its
              detail screen.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>How do I remove the extension?</h2>

            <ol>
              <li>Open Chrome.</li>
              <li>Go to <code>chrome://extensions</code>.</li>
              <li>Find Smart Page Monitor.</li>
              <li>Select <strong>Remove</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
          </article>

          <article class="support-card">
            <h2>Report a problem</h2>

            <p>
              Send an email to:
            </p>

            <p>
              <a href="mailto:seanhart23@gmail.com">
                seanhart23@gmail.com
              </a>
            </p>

            <p>Please include:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>A description of the problem</li>
              <li>The webpage URL, when appropriate</li>
              <li>The error message you received</li>
              <li>Your Chrome version</li>
              <li>Your Smart Page Monitor version</li>
              <li>Steps that reproduce the problem</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Do not send passwords, payment information, or
              other sensitive data.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <aside class="contact-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
          <h2>Still need help?</h2>

          <p>
            Contact the Smart Page Monitor support team by
            email.
          </p>

          <a class="button primary-button full-width-button"
            href="mailto:seanhart23@gmail.com?subject=Smart%20Page%20Monitor%20Support">
            Email support
          </a>

          <p class="small-copy">
            Include the extension version and any error message
            you received.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%- include('./partials/footer.ejs') -%>